      content:
          '**General:** Appears older than stated age. Lying in bed with lights off, facing the wall. Responds to questions but with minimal eye contact. Grooming declined over past 3 days (unshaved, unwashed).\n\n**Neurological (last documented — day 8):**\n- C5 ASIA C: Motor incomplete\n- Upper extremities: Deltoids 3/5 bilateral, biceps 3/5 bilateral, wrist extensors 2/5 bilateral, triceps 2/5 right, 1/5 left, grip developing (trace)\n- Lower extremities: Hip flexors 2/5 bilateral, quad 1/5 right, 2/5 left, ankle dorsiflexion 0/5 bilateral\n- Sensation: Reduced but present (light touch and pinprick) in all dermatomes below C5\n- Rectal exam: Some voluntary anal contraction (confirms motor incomplete)\n\n**Mental Status Today:**\n- Alert and oriented x 3 (person, place, time). Knows he is in rehab.\n- Speech coherent, organized, no tangential thinking\n- Mood: "I just want to go home and be done with it"\n- Affect: flat, tearful intermittently\n- Denies hallucinations or delusions\n- Cognition: Baseline mild cognitive impairment — current testing may be confounded by depression\n\n**PHQ-9 (administered today):** Score 22/27 (severe depression range). Positive on item 9: "Thoughts that you would be better off dead or of hurting yourself" — endorsed as "nearly every day."\n\n**Vital Signs:** BP 148/92 (elevated from baseline, likely pain/distress), HR 88, afebrile.',
